%% Reader question: How does an operator move from bounded evidence to a reversible agent lifecycle decision without ranking unlike mandates?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: reference design; no private agent evaluation, lifecycle decision, or fleet-wide adoption is asserted
stateDiagram-v2
    accTitle: Evidence-backed agent lifecycle state machine
    accDescr: A deployed capability begins with a versioned charter, enters an observation window, and receives a mandate-specific evidence envelope. Missing evidence returns it to observation. Suspected low value enters a safety-checked pause and feed probe that records exclusions, supports emergency abort, restores the capability, and verifies restoration before feeding defined work. Sufficient evidence reaches a human-signed immutable decision to invest, specialize, merge or subsume, repurpose, pause, or retire. The selected decision type remains attached to its implementation. Retirement alone enters a cleanup contract that verifies consumer and work migration, queue disposition, credential revocation, data and memory handling, ownership transfer, and the applicable restore window before termination. Other verified outcomes return to scheduled or event-triggered reassessment.

    [*] --> Chartered: versioned mandate and named consumers
    Chartered --> Observing: open bounded evidence window
    Observing --> EvidenceReview: collect mandate-specific envelope
    EvidenceReview --> Observing: evidence missing or weak
    EvidenceReview --> ProbeReady: suspected low value or underfeeding
    EvidenceReview --> DecisionPending: sufficient evidence and limitations recorded

    state "Reversible pause/feed probe" as Probe {
        [*] --> SafetyCheck
        SafetyCheck --> ExclusionRecorded: unsafe to pause
        ExclusionRecorded --> [*]: preserve exclusion evidence
        SafetyCheck --> PauseWindow: exclusions satisfied and restore tested
        PauseWindow --> Restore: bounded pause completed
        PauseWindow --> EmergencyRestore: unexpected harm and abort
        EmergencyRestore --> Restore
        Restore --> RestoreVerify: exercise restore path
        RestoreVerify --> Restore: service not restored
        RestoreVerify --> FeedWindow: restoration verified
        FeedWindow --> [*]: defined backlog and consumer measured
    }

    ProbeReady --> Probe: preregister outcomes and rollback
    Probe --> EvidenceReview: add probe or exclusion evidence

    state Decision <<choice>>
    DecisionPending --> Decision: human signs immutable decision record
    Decision --> InvestPlan: invest
    Decision --> SpecializePlan: specialize
    Decision --> MergePlan: merge or subsume
    Decision --> RepurposePlan: repurpose
    Decision --> PausePlan: pause
    Decision --> RetirePlan: retire

    InvestPlan --> Implementing: retain invest decision type
    SpecializePlan --> Implementing: retain specialization decision type
    MergePlan --> Implementing: retain lineage and consumer migration obligations
    RepurposePlan --> Implementing: retain old and new charter obligations
    PausePlan --> Implementing: retain pause, safety, and restore obligations

    Implementing --> Verifying: owner, immutable change, rollback or restore
    Verifying --> Implementing: outcome absent, wrong, or unverified
    Verifying --> Reassessment: outcome and enforcement verified
    Reassessment --> Observing: scheduled review or material charter event

    RetirePlan --> RetirementCleanup: approved retirement record
    RetirementCleanup --> RetirementVerify: migrate consumers and work, disposition queues, revoke capabilities, handle data and memory, transfer ownership, preserve restore window
    RetirementVerify --> RetirementCleanup: any postcondition missing or unverified
    RetirementVerify --> [*]: cleanup verified and restore window closed or policy permits termination
